--[[
`nupp` holds admission and layout queries alongside the remaining host,
storage, profiling, random-generator, and text-buffer APIs. Most library code
uses the standard roots directly:

```nupp
local encoded = serde.json.encodevalue({ok = true})
log.info("wrote %d bytes", #encoded)
```

The documented `nupp.host`, `nupp.mem`, `nupp.profile`,
`nupp.random`, and `nupp.text` namespaces retain their current contracts.
I/O, system facts, tasks, types, binary codecs, and serialization use `io`,
`os`, `coroutine`, `types`, `binary`, and `serde` respectively. Private
implementation modules remain beneath `nupp`; application imports use the
documented public module names.

See [standard-library.md](docs/learn/runtime/data/standard-library.md) for the
library overview and [modules.md](docs/learn/language/modules.md) for module
lookup.
]]

const nupp = {}
return nupp
